// Export the inspection, download hashes, attempts, and result.`,explanation:`Deletion confirmation and verification answer different questions. The deleted flag confirms that the API accepted deletion. A follow up retrieval returning four oh four verifies that the session is no longer accessible through that API. A permission error or network timeout cannot verify absence. The page keeps the deletion result if verification is inconclusive and provides a separate verify again action. Physical cleanup can continue asynchronously after the session disappears. Export the checklist and audit result as evidence, without claiming that you observed the underlying container being destroyed.`},{number:`06`,title:`Understand retention and environment ownership`,file:`src/lab30Cleanup.ts`,code:`// openai_hosted: delete the session to request sandbox cleanup.
// Published artifacts survive sandbox expiry.
// Save needed outputs BEFORE deleting the session.
// Removing one artifact leaves its live sandbox file intact.
// self_hosted: coordinate session deletion AND provider shutdown.
// This page accepts only openai_hosted sessions.`,explanation:`Expiration, artifact deletion, and session deletion have different effects. A hosted sandbox can expire when activity and keep alives stop for an hour. That timeout is not configurable and idle time in this page is not an expiry countdown. Published outputs survive that expiry. Deleting one published artifact leaves its live sandbox file intact. Deleting a hosted session requests sandbox cleanup. A self hosted session also needs a separate provider shutdown; deleting its API session does not stop its compute. This lab focuses on OpenAI hosted sessions and does not attempt to stop external infrastructure. Cleanup practice scenarios are synthetic examples, clearly labelled, and never call the API.`}],kM={stoppedInput:!0,retainedOutputs:!0,confirmation:EM.id},AM=[{name:`Completed hosted session can be deleted after retention and confirmation`,run:()=>SM(EM,kM).length===0},...[`in_progress`,`requires_action`,`unknown`].map(e=>({name:`Block session status ${e}`,run:()=>SM({...EM,status:e},kM).length>0})),...[`queued`,`in_progress`,`waiting`].map(e=>({name:`Block latest turn ${e}`,run:()=>SM({...EM,turn:{id:`turn_new`,status:e}},kM).length>0})),...[`completed`,`cancelled`,`failed`].map(e=>({name:`Accept terminal turn ${e}`,run:()=>SM({...EM,turn:{id:`turn_done`,status:e}},kM).length===0})),...[`provisioning`,`pending`,`unknown`].map(e=>({name:`Block environment ${e}`,run:()=>SM({...EM,environmentStatus:e},kM).length>0})),{name:`Pending required action blocks cleanup even if idle`,run:()=>SM({...EM,requiredActions:1},kM).length>0},{name:`Self-hosted compute is outside this lab`,run:()=>SM({...EM,environmentType:`self_hosted`},kM).length>0},{name:`Retention acknowledgement is mandatory`,run:()=>SM(EM,{...kM,retainedOutputs:!1}).length>0},{name:`New input must be stopped`,run:()=>SM(EM,{...kM,stoppedInput:!1}).length>0},{name:`Wrong session confirmation rejected`,run:()=>SM(EM,{...kM,confirmation:`sess_other`}).